# double-stop-thirds: major and minor thirds, both strings plucked together
# Drafted from the recording (envelope onsets + Goertzel harmonic spectrum); confirmed by the bassist.
# 5.50 s: a 50 ms finger blip (C#2) before the first chord; not a note.
# 27.95-29.88 s: D2+F#2 plucked three times without muting in between.
# Thirds on low notes need about 100 ms to separate into two voices (see research notes),
# so the timing tolerance is wider than for single notes.
timing_tolerance 0.15
cents_tolerance 20

6.40 9.10 A1 C#2
10.20 15.15 C2 E2
15.65 26.50 D2 F2
27.95 28.72 D2 F#2
28.75 29.32 D2 F#2
29.35 29.88 D2 F#2
# 30.60-32.20 s: G1+B1 left out: the take is unusable (weakly fretted, off pitch, with open E and
# A ringing louder than the chord), decided with the bassist (ticket 12).
32.20 33.00 F#1 A#1
33.00 33.75 B1 D#2
33.85 36.10 E2 G#2
